{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can install React Query with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://npmjs.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://yarnpkg.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yarn"}]},{"type":"text","value":", or a good ol' "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" via\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://unpkg.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unpkg.com"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"npm","children":[{"type":"text","value":"NPM"}]},{"type":"code","value":"$ npm i react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"yarn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yarn"}]},{"type":"code","value":"$ yarn add react-query","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Query is compatible with React v16.8+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/examples/simple","children":[{"type":"text","value":"simple"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" examples!"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cdn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CDN"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you're not using a module bundler or package manager we also have a global (\"UMD\") build hosted on the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://unpkg.com","children":[{"type":"text","value":"unpkg.com"}]},{"type":"text","value":" CDN. Simply add the following "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script>"},{"type":"text","value":" tag to the bottom of your HTML file:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react-query/dist/react-query.production.min.js\"></script>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you've added this you will have access to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"window.ReactQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" object and its exports."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This installation/usage requires the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://reactjs.org/docs/cdn-links.html","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React CDN script bundles"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to be on the page as well."}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"npm","text":"NPM","level":3},{"id":"yarn","text":"Yarn","level":3},{"id":"cdn","text":"CDN","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou can install React Query with [NPM](https://npmjs.com),\n[Yarn](https://yarnpkg.com), or a good ol' `<script>` via\n[unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com).\n\n### NPM\n```bash\n$ npm i react-query\n```\n### Yarn\n\n```bash\n$ yarn add react-query\n```\n\n\n\nReact Query is compatible with React v16.8+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native.\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [simple](/docs/examples/simple) or [basic](/docs/examples/basic) examples!\n\n### CDN\n\nIf you're not using a module bundler or package manager we also have a global (\"UMD\") build hosted on the [unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com) CDN. Simply add the following `<script>` tag to the bottom of your HTML file:\n\n```html\n<script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react-query/dist/react-query.production.min.js\"></script>\n```\n\nOnce you've added this you will have access to the `window.ReactQuery` object and its exports.\n\n> This installation/usage requires the [React CDN script bundles](https://reactjs.org/docs/cdn-links.html) to be on the page as well.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: installation\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\nYou can install React Query with [NPM](https://npmjs.com),\n[Yarn](https://yarnpkg.com), or a good ol' `<script>` via\n[unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com).\n\n### NPM\n```bash\n$ npm i react-query\n```\n### Yarn\n\n```bash\n$ yarn add react-query\n```\n\n\n\nReact Query is compatible with React v16.8+ and works with ReactDOM and React Native.\n\n> Wanna give it a spin before you download? Try out the [simple](/docs/examples/simple) or [basic](/docs/examples/basic) examples!\n\n### CDN\n\nIf you're not using a module bundler or package manager we also have a global (\"UMD\") build hosted on the [unpkg.com](https://unpkg.com) CDN. Simply add the following `<script>` tag to the bottom of your HTML file:\n\n```html\n<script src=\"https://unpkg.com/react-query/dist/react-query.production.min.js\"></script>\n```\n\nOnce you've added this you will have access to the `window.ReactQuery` object and its exports.\n\n> This installation/usage requires the [React CDN script bundles](https://reactjs.org/docs/cdn-links.html) to be on the page as well.\n"}
